# Not expressible as a prefix, so unjudged under Codex:
# TREE-HAS-A-LIVE-RUN: binds only while a run is live; the process table decides, not a prefix
# BACKGROUND-SHELL-IS-BOUNDED: a property of a background call, which Codex execpolicy does not see
# TRACKED-CITES-NO-EPHEMERAL: judged on what the journal line cites against the repo; a prefix reads neither
# SUBAGENT-NO-PUSH: scoped to subagents; Codex execpolicy has no agent scope
# HEAVY-IS-THE-MAIN-SESSIONS: scoped to subagents; Codex execpolicy has no agent scope
# CONSENT-CODE-FROM-THE-USER: judged on the path it writes or removes, not on the command word
# REPORTS-LIVE-IN-MEMORY: judged on the path it writes or removes, not on the command word
# WRITES-STAY-IN-THE-TREE: judged on the path it writes or removes, not on the command word
# RECURSIVE-DELETE: judged on the path it writes or removes, not on the command word
# WORKTREES-STAY-INSIDE: judged on the path it writes or removes, not on the command word
# FORGE-WRITE-VIA-GH-API: a write is a method flag anywhere in the argv; reads share every prefix
# FORGE-WRITE-VIA-HTTP: a write is a method and a forge URL anywhere in the argv
# STATUS-VIA-DOORS: the forbidden status contexts are an argument value, not a prefix
# HPC-THROUGH-THE-DOOR: judged on the host an ssh/scp/rsync argument names
# REMOTE-WRITE-THROUGH-A-DOOR: judged on the host an ssh/scp/rsync argument names
